0091:     """
0092:     Extend the diagonal blue ray through the grid, reflecting it off red line-segment mirrors.
0093: 
0094:     Input structure
0095:     - Black-background grid with one diagonal 8-connected blue ray seed.
0096:     - Red foreground objects, when present, are straight horizontal or vertical mirror segments.
0097:     - Other foreground bars are transparent to the ray and may be overwritten where the ray crosses them.
0098: 
0099:     Rule
0100:     - Start from the ray seed endpoint whose outward diagonal extension remains inside the grid.
0101:     - Paint the ray continuously in that diagonal direction until it leaves the grid.
0102:     - If the next cell is a red mirror, do not paint it; reflect by flipping the row direction on a horizontal mirror or the column direction on a vertical mirror.
0103: 
0104:     Key insight
0105:     - The non-red bars are decoys: only red bars reflect the diagonal path, while all other crossed cells become blue.
0106:     """
0107:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
0108:     bg = get_bg(g)
0109:     ray_color, seed = _ray_seed(g, bg)
